1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:02,648
This video is for procurement.

2
00:00:02,648 --> 00:00:09,757
You will learn how to prepare requests, send them in shipments, fix a mistake, and manage boxes and custody tools.

3
00:00:10,208 --> 00:00:17,028
Sign in with your name and password. Your account shows only your department: dental or dermatology.

4
00:00:17,479 --> 00:00:24,500
The Requests page shows all requests. Each card is colored by its stage, so you can sort them at a glance.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,951
The chips at the top filter by stage:

6
00:00:26,951 --> 00:00:33,509
with the doctor, ready to prepare, in preparation, partially sent, arrived at the branch, and more.

7
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:41,110
Pick a doctor from the list to see only his requests. You can also filter by branch, clinic or month, or search.

8
00:00:41,561 --> 00:00:46,642
Open a request that is ready. You see each item with the quantity the doctor approved.

9
00:00:46,642 --> 00:00:48,591
This is exactly what you prepare.

10
00:00:49,041 --> 00:00:55,008
Set the status of each item: preparing, waiting for the vendor, or received from the vendor.

11
00:00:55,008 --> 00:00:57,991
The request moves to In preparation by itself.

12
00:00:58,442 --> 00:01:05,021
To send, tick the items and set the quantity for this shipment. You can send part now and the rest later.

13
00:01:05,021 --> 00:01:06,462
Then tap Send shipment.

14
00:01:06,914 --> 00:01:11,872
A box panel opens. The doctor and the branch are filled in from the request.

15
00:01:11,872 --> 00:01:16,373
Change them if the shipment is for sterilization, triage or a clinic.

16
00:01:16,373 --> 00:01:22,374
It tells you if it goes into the doctor's box, or a new box is made. Then tap Load and send.

17
00:01:22,825 --> 00:01:30,625
The card shows exactly what is left. When everything is sent, the request becomes Sent, and the nurse is notified.

18
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:36,550
Sent something by mistake? Tap Undo last step, write the reason, and confirm.

19
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:39,630
Every undo is recorded for the quality team.

20
00:01:40,082 --> 00:01:44,692
From the request details you can print the request, or save it as PDF.

21
00:01:45,143 --> 00:01:50,573
The Boxes page shows where each box is: ready to deliver, at a branch, or empty.

22
00:01:50,573 --> 00:01:58,243
One box for each doctor in each branch. Print the QR stickers, and send the driver tasks link to the driver once.

23
00:01:58,694 --> 00:02:05,394
Need a box back? Tap Request move and choose the place. It appears in the driver's tasks right away.

24
00:02:05,845 --> 00:02:09,525
For older requests, tap Boxes for past requests once.

25
00:02:09,525 --> 00:02:14,315
It makes their boxes and loads any shipment that is not received yet.

26
00:02:14,766 --> 00:02:22,256
Custody is for company tools, like handpieces. Set the standard for each clinic, and handle broken tool reports.

27
00:02:22,708 --> 00:02:28,207
To issue handpieces, tap Issue, choose the tool, and type one serial number per row.

28
00:02:28,207 --> 00:02:33,248
Press Enter or plus for the next one, and Save and add another to keep going.

29
00:02:33,699 --> 00:02:39,576
Complaints shows problems reported on requests. Read them and reply in the request comments.

30
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,429
The quality team closes them.

31
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:47,220
That's it. Prepare approved requests quickly, and send what you have. Thank you!
